{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-77026-r4502092","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Zucchini Bread","sourcePageId":77026,"sourceRevision":"4502092","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-06-08T18:18:58Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Zucchini%20Bread&oldid=4502092","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T16:42:46.279Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Baking recipes","Category:Easy recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for cake","Category:Recipes using all-purpose flour","Category:Recipes using baking powder","Category:Recipes using baking soda","Category:Recipes using egg","Category:Recipes using ground cinnamon","Category:Recipes using vegetable oil","Category:Recipes using white sugar","Category:Recipes using zucchini","Category:Recipes without cooking time"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"0cb7f51ca075d74e757d6c982465fdb84902054952d0d5b33016ad6c94ce317c","sourceWikitext":"{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Cake recipes\n| Servings = 24\n| Difficulty = 2\n}}\n\n{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Bread|Bread]]\n\n'''Zucchini bread''' is a sweet fluffy [[Cookbook:Cake|cake]] or [[Cookbook:Quick Bread|quick bread]] that has zucchini in it. It is delicious. There are many different ways of making it. Here is one. This recipe was derived from the lyrics of a song by a band called Chuga Chuga, from Michigan/Washington, DC, USA. They broke up in 2006.\n\n== Ingredients ==\n*3 [[Cookbook:Cup|cups]] [[Cookbook:All-purpose flour|all-purpose flour]]\n*1 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|teaspoon]] [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n*1 teaspoon [[Cookbook:Baking Soda|baking soda]]\n*1 teaspoon [[Cookbook:Baking Powder|baking powder]]\n*3 teaspoons ground [[Cookbook:Cinnamon|cinnamon]]\n*3 [[Cookbook:Egg|eggs]]\n*1 cup [[Cookbook:Vegetable oil|vegetable oil]]\n*2¼ cups [[Cookbook:White Sugar|white sugar]]\n*3 teaspoons [[Cookbook:Vanilla|vanilla]] extract\n*2 cups [[Cookbook:Grater|grated]] [[Cookbook:Zucchini|zucchini]]\n\n== Procedure ==\n\n# Grease and flour two 8 x 4-[[Cookbook:Inch|inch]] [[Cookbook:Loaf Pan|loaf pans]]. Preheat [[Cookbook:Oven|oven]] to 325°F.\n# [[Cookbook:Sifting|Sift]] together flour, salt, baking powder, baking soda, and cinnamon in a bowl.\n# [[Cookbook:Beating|Beat]] eggs, oil, vanilla, and sugar together in a large bowl.\n# Add sifted ingredients to the creamed mixture, and beat well. Stir in zucchini until well combined.\n# Pour batter into prepared pans.\n# [[Cookbook:Baking|Bake]] for 40 minutes to 1 hour, or until tester inserted into the center comes out clean.\n# Cool in pan for 20 minutes. Remove from pan and completely cool.\n\n[[Category:Recipes for cake]]\n[[Category:Recipes using zucchini]]\n[[Category:Baking recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using egg]]\n[[Category:Recipes using baking powder]]\n[[Category:Recipes using baking soda]]\n[[Category:Recipes using white sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using ground cinnamon]]\n[[Category:Recipes using all-purpose flour]]\n[[Category:Recipes using vegetable oil]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Zucchini Bread","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":"24","ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"3 cups all-purpose flour","sourceText":"3 cups all-purpose flour","amountText":"3 cups all-purpose flour","am